  "meta": {
    "title": "A/B Drive (graph twin)",
    "notes": "Golden twin of main.py (graph format 1.1): the same parameters, the same derivations and the same operations in the same order. main.py stays the oracle; y4d-spec --parity compares the two at the defaults and at every preset. The e_end clamp is a ternary pair; the belt levels and rear runs are ternaries on mirrored; the right (A) drive is body.mirror('YZ') as reflect YZ chosen by select on mirrored. FROZEN VALUES: the three roof arms (_bar) take their lengths and angles from hypot/atan2, which the expression dialect does not have. Their inputs are the script's conventions (POST_K/POST_Q/POST_S centres, K_XY, U_Q, U_S, the rear runs) and mirrored only, so the derived values k_len, k_ang, q_len, q_ang, s_len, s_ang are computed from the script's conventions by hypot/atan2 and frozen as exact float64 literals (a ternary on mirrored where they depend on it). A change to those conventions in main.py breaks parity at every preset, so drift cannot pass unnoticed. Cited facts as main.py: NEMA 17 face 42.3, bolts 31, pilot 22 (keystone nema-17-48mm); GT2 20T belt mid-plane 8 above face A, seat 2; F695 stack 10 (DIN 988 + NSK); GT2 20T idler 9 (Motedis); 2020 profile 20, lip 2, pilot 4.2 (MISUMI HFS5); rail setback 25 (guide p. 88); M5 head 9.5 (ISO 7380-1). Every other number is a labelled convention of main.py."
  },
